cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "dish2ecg: corrected repolarization endpoints from hiPSC-CM and clinical ECG data"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it and the underlying datasets."
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-02"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  dish2ecg applies one correction cascade - rate correction, baseline
  subtraction, vehicle or placebo subtraction, and a mixed-effects
  concentration-response model - symmetrically to human induced pluripotent stem
  cell derived cardiomyocyte field-potential recordings and to clinical 12-lead
  ECG data, so that an in-vitro concentration-response and a clinical
  concentration-QTc relationship can be compared on a shared free-Cmax scale.
  Every derived value carries the provenance of the corrections that produced it,
  and in-vitro endpoints are structurally prevented from being reported as QT
  intervals.
keywords:
  - cardiac safety
  - QT interval
  - hiPSC-CM
  - CiPA
  - proarrhythmia
  - field potential duration
  - concentration-QTc
